Z||000000||count_iblis||10-06-2000||09:41 PM||||there is a Quad 4 engine for sale it is <P>rebuilt with 20,000 miles on it.  Now my<P>question is is it worth replacing the v6 in<P>the 87 gt .  Also would i be losing torque?  <P>I have the slightest clue about torque.  <P>What is the hp and torque of the Quad 4?  <P>Also there is a 3800 engine for 350.00 but i <P>havent contacted the owner yet to see if it <P>is the supercharged one or not.  Just need <P>some answers.  I hardly ever get respones on <P>my posts so please respond to this.  <P>Thanks,  <P><BR>COUNT<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||pherder||10-06-2000||10:05 PM||||I have a HO Quad 4 in my 88 Coupe.  It is rated @ 180 hp.  I don't know the torque but it is much less than the V6's.  <P>It is gutless below 3000 rpm.<P>It screams over 3000 rpm and will out run a "stock" 2.8 V6 <B>ONCE</B> it gets in the upper rpm range (7400 rpm red line with the special W41 chip.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)<P>Driving around town isn't much fun ... getting 35 mpg is    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>It is a <B>LOT</B> of work to get it in the Fiero (you <B>HAVE</B> to use the transaxle that comes with the Quad 4 since it has a much different bolt pattern.<P>I was going to take it to the drags tonight but with 40 degree weather and wind chill, I wimped out.<P>See pictures of my HO Quad 4 project @<BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=208525&a=1537447" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=208525&a=1537447</A> <P>BTW, I was going to make this my daily driver but will now put my efforts into my 88 GT with a stock rebuild of the V6 and an automatic.  Much easier to drive around town with.<P>Paul<P><p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 10-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||baldlobo||10-06-2000||11:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pherder:<BR><B>I have a HO Quad 4 in my 88 Coupe.  It is rated @ 180 hp.  I don't know the torque but it is much less than the V6's.  <P>It is gutless below 3000 rpm.<P>It screams over 3000 rpm and will out run a "stock" 2.8 V6 [b]ONCE</B> it gets in the upper rpm range (7400 rpm red line with the special W41 chip.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)<P>Driving around town isn't much fun ... getting 35 mpg is     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>It is a <B>LOT</B> of work to get it in the Fiero (you <B>HAVE</B> to use the transaxle that comes with the Quad 4 since it has a much different bolt pattern.<P>I was going to take it to the drags tonight but with 40 degree weather and wind chill, I wimped out.<P>See pictures of my HO Quad 4 project @<BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=208525&a=1537447" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=208525&a=1537447</A> <P>BTW, I was going to make this my daily driver but will now put my efforts into my 88 GT with a stock rebuild of the V6 and an automatic.  Much easier to drive around town with.<P>Paul<P>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 10-06-2000).][/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>you've go one he!! of a nice car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000003||88formula||10-06-2000||11:07 PM||||Torque is what launches you off the line. $350 for a 3800 engine is a great deal especially if it's the series two motor (205 hp). The 3800 engine N.A. or S.C. would be more reliable and faster than a Quad four engine. The quad four engine is very light and would give you a better handling fiero.||||reg||1
